description:
FILED s514b (Opus, 2026-10-10), found by the s514b sweep (perl-tests/local.t row 267 'is($FETCH, 0)' passes on main only BY ACCIDENT: the FETCH counter is never incremented).

Reproducer (scratch/s514b/pr/m4b.pl), perl 5.40.3 vs main 134ca17f:

    {
        my $STORE = my $FETCH = 0;
        package TieHash;
        sub TIEHASH { bless $_[1], $_[0] }
        sub FETCH   { ++$FETCH; 42 }
        sub STORE   { ++$STORE }
        package main;
        tie my %hash, 'TieHash', {};
        my $x = $hash{a}; $hash{b} = 1;
        print "$STORE $FETCH\n";      # perl 1 1   PCL 1 0
    }

Emission: `sub FETCH` reads `TieHash::$FETCH` while the decl is `$FETCH` (the first `my`, $STORE, is correctly promoted to $STORE__file__0).  So _requalify_block_globals_after_pkg_switch (Pl/Parser2.pm, run before the scans) does not see the SECOND declarator of a chained `my $a = my $b` as a declaration.  Rule 11: the 'which tokens does this statement declare' question is _declarator_syms' -- check whether the requalify pass asks it.  Guard: the reproducer + local.t row 267 must then pass for the right reason (FETCH counter really 0 in local.t since the tie there is never read).
